IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `or336-nouns`
IMPORT `or336-art336a`
IMPORT `or336-art336b`

-- Traces of the three regulative rules of Art. 336a and 336b OR (layer 1).
--
-- A #TRACE prints an outcome but asserts nothing, and a DEONTIC value cannot
-- be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT. So each trace carries, on the line
-- above it, an `-- EXPECT:` comment written from the German text before the
-- file was run, and check-traces.py compares the printed outcome with it on
-- both stable builds (FULFILLED; BREACH; RESIDUAL = the obligation still
-- stands). check.sh does not see a trace, so check-traces.py is part of the
-- checks (NOTES.md says so).
--
-- The clock counts DAYS. Day 0 is the day the notice was given (Art. 336b(1))
-- or the day the employment ended (Art. 336b(2)); the 336a(1) duty names no
-- time at all.

§ `Traces of the regulative rules`

§§ `Art 336a(1): the party giving the notice must pay the compensation`

-- "hat der anderen Partei eine Entschädigung auszurichten": paid, whenever it is paid (the text names no time limit).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336a(1) the duty to pay compensation` Employer AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `pay the compensation` AT 5

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336a(1) the duty to pay compensation` Employee AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `pay the compensation` AT 400

-- not paid yet: the duty stands (no deadline, so no breach however long the wait).
-- EXPECT: RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 336a(1) the duty to pay compensation` Employer AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 1000

§§ `Art 336b(1): the party that received the notice must object in writing by the end of the notice period (30 days after the notice)`

-- the day before the end of the notice period.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employee 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `object in writing to the notice` AT 29

-- the day the notice period ends: "längstens bis zum Ende der Kündigungsfrist".
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employee 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `object in writing to the notice` AT 30

-- the day after.
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employee 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `object in writing to the notice` AT 31

-- the party that received the notice is the employer: the same rule from the other side.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employer 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `object in writing to the notice` AT 30

-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employer 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

-- the clock stops on the last day: the duty still stands.
-- EXPECT: RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 336b(1) the duty to object` Employer 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 30

§§ `Art 336b(2): the action within 180 days after the end of the employment`

-- the day before the 180th day.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employee AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `bring an action` AT 179

-- the 180th day: "innert 180 Tagen nach Beendigung des Arbeitsverhältnisses".
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employee AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `bring an action` AT 180

-- the 181st day: the claim is forfeited ("ist der Anspruch verwirkt").
-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employee AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employee DOES `bring an action` AT 181

-- the party that received the notice is the employer: the same rule from the other side.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employer AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Employer DOES `bring an action` AT 180

-- EXPECT: BREACH
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employer AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 181

-- the clock stops on the 180th day: the window is still open.
-- EXPECT: RESIDUAL
#TRACE `Art 336b(2) the window to bring the action` Employer AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 180
